<title>USA: Motorola in deal to make UK intelligent car.</title>
<headline>Motorola in deal to make UK intelligent car.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Tuesday it has teamed with General Motors Corp's Vauxhall division, Vodafone Group Plc and Britain's Automobile Association to build the Vauxhall Onstar system.</p>
<p>The system is an in-vehicle communications system which lets drivers call for emergency help, roadside assistance and other services.  It will lead to GM's first &quot;intelligent car&quot; in Britain, Motorola said.</p>
<p>Trials are scheduled to begin by next month, and the system is expected to be available in autumn.</p>
<p>The Vauxhall system uses Global Positioning System technology and a custom-made mobile phone, which operates through the car's stereo system.</p>
<p>Motorola provides wireless communications, semiconductors and advanced electronic systems, components and services.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
